    <section class="msc-learn-key-terms" aria-labelledby="MscGuide068Terms"><h2 id="MscGuide068Terms">Key Terms</h2><dl><div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Industry leader</dt><dd>Person or organization with influence through commercial, organizational, funding, technical, policy, media, or infrastructure roles.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Protocol authority</dt><dd>Claimed power to determine Bitcoin consensus; industry status does not grant it.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Product default</dt><dd>Preselected application behavior that can shape users without becoming a Bitcoin protocol rule.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Infrastructure ownership</dt><dd>Control over operational systems such as exchanges, custodians, mining facilities, APIs, or distribution.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Capital allocation</dt><dd>Decision about where money, grants, equipment, or organizational resources are directed.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Regulatory access</dt><dd>Ability to communicate with or influence policymakers and regulators.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Conflict of interest</dt><dd>Interest that may affect or appear to affect a person’s responsibilities or judgment.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Concentration risk</dt><dd>Risk created when many users or systems depend on a small number of providers or decision centers.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Vendor dependence</dt><dd>Reliance on a third party for a critical service, interface, credential, or data source.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Regulatory capture</dt><dd>Risk that regulated institutions shape rules for their own benefit rather than the public purpose.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Exit</dt><dd>Ability to leave a service, export assets or data, switch software, or build a competing system.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Failure domain</dt><dd>Shared component whose failure can affect multiple apparently separate services.</dd></div>
<div class="msc-learn-term"><dt>Accountability</dt><dd>Ability to evaluate decisions through evidence, disclosure, governance, and correction.</dd></div></dl></section>
